+# Daily Grind performance monitoring
+
+`scripts/performance-monitor.js` observes browser-reported
+`interaction-contentful-paint` entries for the navigation bar, Order Now, and
+Seasonal Favorites cards. Durations are milliseconds from the initiating input
+to presentation of each progressively larger contentful paint, including
+asynchronous updates. Event Timing interaction IDs provide attribution; captured
+input timestamps also cover fast interactions omitted by Event Timing.
+
+It also observes `soft-navigation` entries for client-side view changes, recording
+first contentful paint duration and the largest contentful paint duration. Route
+reports finalize on the next soft navigation, page hide, or backgrounding. Early
+paint candidates are seeded with `getLargestInteractionContentfulPaint()`, and
+later candidates are matched by interaction ID, rather than navigation ID.
+
+Consume reports without modifying the UI:
+
+```js
+window.addEventListener('daily-grind:performance', ({ detail }) => {
+  // Forward detail to your analytics service here.
+});
+window.dailyGrindPerformance.getReports(); // Latest 100 reports
+window.dailyGrindPerformance.support; // Browser capability flags
+```
+
+Reports include stable region identifiers, interaction IDs, durations, and
+destination paths. They omit query strings and DOM text. No analytics endpoint
+is configured, and reports are only retained in memory.
+
+These APIs have limited browser availability. Unsupported observers are skipped;
+clicks without a contentful update produce no paint metric. The existing links
+perform full document navigations, so they do not generate soft navigation
+metrics. This instrumentation does not intercept links or add a router, and
+does not measure destination documents that do not load this script.
+
+API reference: [Chrome interaction and soft-navigation paint timing](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance/guides/performance/interaction-paint-timing).
+
+Run the isolated observer tests with `node --test tests/performance-monitor.test.cjs`.
+They simulate browser entries without starting a server or browser.
